34,2,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Minato,,"It seems the treasurer spends a lot of time chasing money for individual sessions, and some people struggle to pay the full renewal at once.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The ledger shows that seventy percent of our costs are fixed, like hall hire and insurance, regardless of how many people actually attend.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Minako,,"Past attempts at named grades caused friction and discouraged some members, while many potential joiners are deterred by the commitment of a full annual fee.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,"It's worrying; turnout for weekday meetings dropped significantly after the summer outings' door charges, and some quieter members feel uneasy about the cost per visit.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"The data confirms my suspicions: a small group of people are doing almost all the attending and the actual work, while many others barely show up at all.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Ryuji, if most costs are fixed, does that mean we can't really lower the base fee without risking the club's stability?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"Exactly. If we shift too much to a pay-as-you-go system, we might not cover the essentials. We cannot afford to guess the figures this time.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Minako,,"We must also consider that a rigid structure might alienate newcomers, as the taster forms suggest they are wary of a large upfront commitment.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"That's exactly why the door charges were such a mistake. People stopped feeling like the evenings belonged to them, and now they're hesitating to even walk through the door.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,It is unfair that the same few people are carrying the club while others pay a pittance for the privilege of barely appearing. We need a system that reflects actual usage.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Minato,,"But if we make it too complex to reflect usage, will that just make the treasurer's job even harder? I'm worried about the workload.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"That is a valid concern, Minato. If we implement a system with too many variables, we risk burning out whoever takes over the books.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Minako,,"We should be careful not to create a system that makes membership feel like a transaction, as that could further discourage the drift-in culture we've traditionally valued.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,"I agree with Minako. If we make it too transactional, we lose the welcoming atmosphere. We need something that feels inclusive but doesn't make people hesitate to join.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"Inclusive is all well and good, but we can't ignore the resentment building among the regulars. A flat fee essentially subsidizes those who never show up.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Minato,,I just hope we can find a balance that doesn't make the treasurer's life a nightmare while still being fair to everyone.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"We must ensure the final figure is based on the fixed costs I found in the ledger, rather than just trying to please everyone.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Minako,,"We should also keep in mind that any system we choose will be visible to all members, so we must avoid creating a hierarchy that feels exclusionary.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,I just want us to make sure that whatever we decide doesn't make people feel like they have to calculate the value of their presence before they decide to come.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,Then we are at an impasse. We cannot ignore the fact that a handful of people are doing all the heavy lifting while others pay nothing for the effort.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
