60,3,1,talk,Minato,,"Now that we have the options, I'm worried that Activity-Based Charging would make the treasurer's job impossible given how much time is already spent chasing small payments.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"I agree with Minato. Given that seventy percent of our costs are fixed, a Flat Annual Fee is the most stable and predictable way to ensure we cover our essentials.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Minako,,Tiered Membership seems risky because the historical records show that named grades created friction and made some members feel less inclined to participate.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,May,,I'm leaning toward the Flat Annual Fee too; Activity-Based Charging sounds like it would just bring back that hesitation I saw with the summer outings.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,A Flat Annual Fee is simply unfair to the regulars. Tiered Membership is the only way to acknowledge different levels of commitment and usage without making every single visit a transaction.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@Shunichi, but wouldn't Tiered Membership just create the hierarchy Minako is worried about? I'm still very concerned about the workload for the treasurer if we have multiple levels to track.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Shunichi"",""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Minato, you're right. Managing multiple tiers and the associated calculations for mid-year joiners would be a logistical burden. A Flat Annual Fee is the only option that provides financial certainty and simplicity.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Minako,,"I must agree with Ryuji and Minato. Tiered Membership risks creating a visible divide between members, which could damage the inclusive atmosphere we've worked so hard to maintain.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,May,,"I agree. If we have tiers, people will start comparing themselves to others, and that's exactly the kind of pressure that makes the quieter members feel uneasy.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"You are all prioritizing a vague ""atmosphere"" over the actual reality of the club's operation. If we don't address the imbalance of effort and cost, we'll lose the regulars who actually keep this place running.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Minato,,"@Shunichi, I understand it feels unfair, but if the treasurer quits because the system is too complex, then nobody wins and the club might fail entirely.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"The risk of financial instability and administrative collapse outweighs the perceived unfairness of a flat fee. We need a system that is sustainable and guaranteed, not one that risks the club's existence.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Minako,,"Furthermore, the taster forms showed that a high upfront cost is a barrier. A single, fair flat fee is easier to communicate and less intimidating than a complex tiered system.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,May,,"Exactly. If we make it too complicated or tiered, we're just adding more barriers. A flat fee is simple, welcoming, and doesn't make people overthink their value every time they visit.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"It seems I am the only one concerned with the people actually doing the work. If you insist on simplicity over fairness, you are simply choosing to ignore the resentment of your most loyal members.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Minato,,"I'm sorry, Shunichi, but I have to vote for the Flat Annual Fee to protect the treasurer's time and the club's stability.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,I vote for the Flat Annual Fee. It is the only rational choice to ensure our fixed costs are covered without relying on guesswork or administrative chaos.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Minako,,"I vote for the Flat Annual Fee, as it avoids the friction of tiers and maintains the inclusive spirit of the club.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,May,,I vote for the Flat Annual Fee; it's the best way to make sure everyone feels welcome without hesitating at the door.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,I vote for Tiered Membership. I cannot in good conscience support a system that continues to exploit the most dedicated members for the benefit of those who barely contribute.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
